      price: rop_logic is not priced by gt1030 (not measured): unavailable
      pipeline: VkPipelineColorBlendStateCreateInfo: logicOpEnable, logicOp = VK_LOGIC_OP_OR (the logicOp feature); an R32_UINT colour attachment; one point per contribution, its position the cell, its colour s
  not in any price: the draw's setup (a render pass, the pipeline, one vertex per contribution) and reading the target back
> cnt(d: u8) = d + 1
> rop cnt
rop cnt: cnt = d + 1, applied once per fragment (d the cell's value)
  order: every fragment applies the same update: their order is immaterial
  fixed-function states that compute it (each a proposal: the pipeline changes):
  stencil op: VK_STENCIL_OP_INCREMENT_AND_WRAP on the 8-bit stencil value: d + 1
      checked on every point of the domain
      price: rop_stencil is not priced by gt1030 (not measured): unavailable
      pipeline: VkStencilOpState: passOp = VK_STENCIL_OP_INCREMENT_AND_WRAP, writeMask = 0xff; a stencil attachment (S8_UINT); one fragment per contribution, its position the cell
  occlusion query: VK_QUERY_TYPE_OCCLUSION, precise, around the draw: the fragments that pass, counted: d + 1
      holds where every contribution updates the same cell: a query counts a whole draw (more cells: a draw and a query each)
      the update is d + 1 (checked on every point of the domain); a precise occlusion query counts every sample that passes the fragment tests, which with no depth or stencil test and one sample a point is one a contribution; read as 64 bits the count is exact, and adding it to the cell wraps in u8 as the update does
      price: rop_query is not priced by gt1030 (not measured): unavailable
      pipeline: VkQueryPoolCreateInfo: queryType = VK_QUERY_TYPE_OCCLUSION; vkCmdBeginQuery with VK_QUERY_CONTROL_PRECISE_BIT (the occlusionQueryPrecise feature) around a draw of one point per contribution, anywhere (no depth or stencil test, one sample a pixel); vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResults with VK_QUERY_RESULT_64_BIT into a buffer, and the cell's d + count once after the draw
  not in any price: the draw's setup (a render pass, the pipeline, one vertex per contribution) and reading the target back
