> mx(s: f32, d: f32) = max(s, d)
> rop mx
rop mx: mx = max(s, d), applied once per fragment (s what a fragment brings, d the cell's value)
  order: the result does not depend on the order of the fragments: max is associative and commutative on floats other than NaN (up to the sign of a zero)
  fixed-function states that compute it (each a proposal: the pipeline changes):
  blending: VK_BLEND_OP_MAX on a float target (R32_SFLOAT): max(s, d) (the factors are not used)
      holds where neither value is NaN; the sign of a zero result may differ
      the same operation: the result is one of the two values, nothing rounds
      price: rop_blend is not priced by gt1030 (not measured): unavailable
      pipeline: VkPipelineColorBlendAttachmentState: blendEnable, colorBlendOp = VK_BLEND_OP_MAX; an R32_SFLOAT colour attachment; one point per contribution, its position the cell, its colour s
  not in any price: the draw's setup (a render pass, the pipeline, one vertex per contribution) and reading the target back
